Description: read the soundtrack from a FLAC file with libsndfile
 The Debian package ships the precalculated soundtrack compressed as FLAC.
 It used to be decoded back to WAV by the postinst script, which left an
 untracked file in /usr/share and removed a file shipped by the package.
 The intro now decodes the FLAC file directly with libsndfile, into the
 same 32-bit float buffer as before.
Author: Nicolas HOUDELOT <nicolas@demosdebs.org>
Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
